{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092083-so-siochain","id":1092083,"title":"So, Siochain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T13:42:20-07:00","id":1092083,"title":"So, Siochain","content":"Looking to move past something of a bummer of a conversation, and remembered this as one of my big interests.<br /> <br /> This particular &quot;enlightened changeling&quot; state of affairs has always felt like something just tantalizingly out of reach as far as getting details on it. There's been the occasional npc here and there noted as being in such a state, there's even a dauntain who achieved it, but then fell hard from it later (which I always found interesting and terrifying as a concept, even if the execution wasn't great). It's been one of my big hopes to get more details on it in a book someday.<br /> <br /> There's just something really fascinating to me about the idea of having somehow come fully into both mortal and fae states of being. What would that look like? What would the mindset resemble?<br /> <br /> I know, I know, lack of detail means it can be whatever you want, but even Golconda in Vampire gets more of a fleshing out for what it might entail and how to go about it.<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder, how have you guys treated it in your games? Have you used it? Let players try for it? Hash out any kind of system for what it would mean to achieve it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}